00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.640
with us tomorrow?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.000
I'd love to.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.200
a charity. Blessed are the peacemakers

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.280
and we are in need of a peacemaker.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.560
What's it all about?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.980
The usual thing. What?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.020
Women? Father, please. In this case

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.360
it happens to have been something else.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.040
All right, take me out. It's time to go and

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.900
feed the dogs. I began it,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.600
I'm afraid, by objecting to a brother.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.540
That made Emily object to me,

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.920
violently, after which we both

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.230
lost our temples. Utterly senseless

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.110
of course, but then such is life, unfortunately.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.990
It needn't be. No,

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:00.000
I suppose not. If I were a little

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.780
less impatient. And Emily could be more understanding. Then each of us would be somebody

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:11.300
