Henry didn't give her the coffee, did he?

01:11:46.420 --> 01:11:48.290
I really don't know.

01:11:49.610 --> 01:11:50.550
Somebody must have.

01:11:53.110 --> 01:11:55.830
Anyhow, it's of no importance, is it, seeing that everything's been proved?

01:11:57.220 --> 01:11:58.570
Quite.

01:12:00.800 --> 01:12:01.120
Quite.

01:12:01.380 --> 01:12:03.760
I wish it were all over.

01:12:05.080 --> 01:12:05.900
All over?

01:12:07.690 --> 01:12:12.500
You seem to think this business is like something in the movies or in a novel.

01:12:14.150 --> 01:12:17.770
You seem to think it has an ending at 8 o'clock next Friday week, to be precise.

01:12:18.590 --> 01:12:21.080
I don't know what you're driving at.

01:12:22.160 --> 01:12:25.840
I'm driving at some way to make you sleep.

01:12:32.520 --> 01:12:35.060
Well, this has been a very interesting talk, Dr. Liver.

01:12:35.970 --> 01:12:39.150
But whether it's going to cure my insomnia, that's another question.

01:12:40.170 --> 01:12:42.390
Personally, I put more faith in sleeping tablets.

01:12:42.480 --> 01:12:46.860
Janet, do you remember meeting a young Dr. Fardin at my house this spring?

01:12:47.290 --> 01:12:47.910
Yes.

01:12:48.370 --> 01:12:52.660
I've known him ever since he was a boy. He's a very nice fellow. Kind, sensible, conscientious.

01:12:52.960 --> 01:12:55.550
And he's turned out to be a first-class psychiatrist.

01:12:55.630 --> 01:12:57.430
No, thanks. I don't want to go to a psychiatrist.

01:12:57.510 --> 01:12:59.750
- You want to get well, don't you? - I'm not ill!

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:02.930
- Not that way, I know you.

01:13:02.930 --> 01:13:04.430
You're going to tell them I'm mad,

01:13:04.430 --> 01:13:05.850
and then they'll lock me up and torture me

01:13:05.850 --> 01:13:07.370
until I say things.

01:13:07.370 --> 01:13:09.830
It's a plot, everyone's plotting against me.

01:13:09.830 --> 01:13:12.130
- Nobody's plotting anything.

01:13:12.130 --> 01:13:13.230
- That's a lie.

01:13:13.230 --> 01:13:14.700
You said it yourself.

01:13:14.700 --> 01:13:16.730
You want me to go to a doctor for mad people.

01:13:16.730 --> 01:13:17.770
- If I don't want to do any harm,

01:13:17.770 --> 01:13:19.130
he'll just ask you a few questions

01:13:19.130 --> 01:13:20.770
and find out what's on your mind.

01:13:20.770 --> 01:13:23.510
- I've told you again and again.

01:13:23.510 --> 01:13:25.070
I haven't anything on my mind.

01:13:25.070 --> 01:13:27.040
It's just that I can't sleep.

01:13:27.040 --> 01:13:28.870
- But he'll help you with that.

01:13:28.870 --> 01:13:30.000
He'll put you to sleep, Phil.

01:13:30.060 --> 01:13:36.020
- Do you mean he'll hypnotize me? - Well, what's so alarming about that?

01:13:36.020 --> 01:13:41.190
Send me to sleep and then make me say a lot of things I don't want to say?

01:13:41.190 --> 01:13:46.170
And I shan't even know I've said them? No! No, I won't! I won't!

01:13:46.170 --> 01:13:48.170
- Janet, be reasonable. - Don't touch me!

01:13:48.170 --> 01:13:51.170
- Janet! - I'll kill you, do you understand?

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:02.000
I dispense to see you, Moirier.

01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:23.900
I don't mind us. Carry on as if we weren't here.

01:14:23.900 --> 01:14:25.900
It's difficult to believe that you are quite real.

01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:30.000
Nothing is quite real anymore.

01:14:38.320 --> 01:14:44.720
When one thinks about time, draining away like blood from a wound, and you can't stop

01:14:44.720 --> 01:14:46.250
it.

01:14:46.250 --> 01:14:53.660
It just goes on, quietly flowing until there isn't any more, and then you're dead.

01:14:53.660 --> 01:14:54.660
Was that half past three?

01:14:54.660 --> 01:15:00.000
Yes, that was half past three.

01:15:04.410 --> 01:15:12.300
12 makes 16 and 24, 40 hours, a little more than 40 hours.

01:15:13.060 --> 01:15:18.320
It's like being at the edge of a huge black pit and something is pushing you from behind.

01:15:19.590 --> 01:15:23.170
Perhaps it would be more bearable if it made some kind of sense.

01:15:24.490 --> 01:15:27.350
If at least one could believe that there is such thing as justice.

01:15:27.810 --> 01:15:28.370
There is.

01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:46.690
journey. I didn't do it. I swear by all that is sacred. Sacred? What is sacred? Do you

01:15:46.690 --> 01:15:51.790
remember that night? That night when there was a thunderstorm. You talked about Benjamin

01:15:51.790 --> 01:15:56.670
Franklin, you know, sending up his little kite to attract the lightning. Sort of scientific,

01:15:56.930 --> 01:16:00.000
practical joke. Well, sometimes

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:07.060
the joke comes off sometimes the lightning comes down the string and then well people get killed

01:16:07.060 --> 01:16:14.480
get killed and whose fault is it they get killed the fault of the lightning or the fault of the

01:16:14.480 --> 01:16:20.160
little man who thought it would be such fun to play tricks with it understand what you mean

01:16:20.160 --> 01:16:30.000
well don't try just imagine a little group of boys at school what does your father do

01:16:31.020 --> 01:16:32.020
Oh, he's a barrister.

01:16:32.900 --> 01:16:35.140
And yours, he's an engineer.

01:16:36.250 --> 01:16:39.200
And yours, my father's dead.

01:16:40.020 --> 01:16:41.400
He died before I was born.

01:16:42.310 --> 01:16:44.530
