01:16:45.900 --> 01:16:47.090
My next tomb.

01:16:48.650 --> 01:16:50.920
Did I ever ask for mercy?

01:16:52.650 --> 01:16:54.130
Did you ever think of showing it?

01:16:54.940 --> 01:16:55.320
Never.

01:16:56.590 --> 01:16:59.330
I never said anything when you amused yourself at my expense.

01:16:59.640 --> 01:17:00.000
Sure.

01:17:01.120 --> 01:17:07.400
that? What else were you doing all those years? Beckoning me on, calling me to you, and then

01:17:07.400 --> 01:17:12.600
at last when I came to you, you hit me across the face and then ran off to have a good laugh

01:17:12.600 --> 01:17:20.320
for that filthy little beast. You say that? Yes, how dare I. Do what you like, but never

01:17:20.320 --> 01:17:27.860
say. That's shocking, that's disgusting. How old was she, Henry, when she first started

01:17:27.860 --> 01:17:30.000
doing these things? Eighteen?

01:17:30.830 --> 01:17:35.490
Seventeen, slurring and pawing, and you call it love.

01:17:36.020 --> 01:17:37.940
Love, filth, that's what it was.

01:17:38.300 --> 01:17:40.980
And you threw the filth in my face and then roared with laughter.

01:17:46.250 --> 01:17:47.910
Why don't you go on laughing, Henry?

01:17:49.810 --> 01:17:55.040
Laugh, laugh, this is all part of the same joke.

01:17:56.440 --> 01:17:58.460
Don't you understand?

01:17:59.290 --> 01:17:59.670
Johnny.

01:18:03.160 --> 01:18:06.910
Forty hours was more, that's all.

01:18:08.780 --> 01:18:11.400
And you asked me to lunch on your 80th birthday.

01:18:13.660 --> 01:18:14.800
Why don't you laugh?

01:18:18.220 --> 01:18:19.400
Goodbye, Henry.

01:18:34.220 --> 01:18:36.390
- She was the one. She did it. - Keep quiet.

01:18:36.390 --> 01:18:38.110
But she told me. She confessed.

01:18:38.110 --> 01:18:42.680
Janet! Janet! Janet!

01:18:42.680 --> 01:18:44.760
But she's the murderer. She told me.

01:18:44.760 --> 01:18:47.670
But it's true. I swear it is letting me go.

01:18:47.670 --> 01:18:50.150
- That's better now. Sit down. - Tell her to come back.

01:18:50.150 --> 01:18:51.630
Make her say it again in front of Wilton.

01:18:51.630 --> 01:18:55.190
- Keep quiet. - Let me go. Let me go. Sit down.

01:19:02.330 --> 01:19:13.870
time passes slowly. Not for him. Eight o'clock at Wandsworth. There but for the grace of God

01:19:13.870 --> 01:19:23.650
goes James Libbard. And there but for the grace of God goes Janet Spence. Happily there was the

